{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792935334,"nonce":"4z+St0QeuClYl65UHjZurgCGB+c=","message":"Revised with RayDE: stopping a job is SIGKILL (HashLink Process.kill), so serve relies on no signal handler. It keeps no lock file, binds with SO_REUSEADDR so the next serve takes the port at once, and keeps its watcher and HTTP server in process. A compiler it starts (haxe, a plugin's cargo build) dies with it on Linux (PR_SET_PDEATHSIG); on macOS a stray one finishes on its own and blocks nothing. The serving record goes to the --diagnostics file, not stdout.","files":null}]}